# DreamPicoPort (OrangeFox86) -- a Dreamcast controller over USB.
# Codes confirmed by capture on 2026-10-04, not guessed.
#
# All four adapter ports share this one name, so this file applies to every port.
# Without it OpenJVS falls back to generic-joystick, which sends BTN_EAST to
# CONTROLLER_BUTTON_D -- putting Dreamcast B on BUTTON_4 instead of BUTTON_2, so
# Virtua Tennis lob would not work.

BTN_SOUTH CONTROLLER_BUTTON_A
BTN_EAST  CONTROLLER_BUTTON_B
BTN_NORTH CONTROLLER_BUTTON_C
BTN_WEST  CONTROLLER_BUTTON_D
BTN_START CONTROLLER_BUTTON_START

# D-pad. Reports -1/0/1, which is what the axis-to-two-buttons path expects.
ABS_HAT0X CONTROLLER_BUTTON_LEFT CONTROLLER_BUTTON_RIGHT
ABS_HAT0Y CONTROLLER_BUTTON_UP CONTROLLER_BUTTON_DOWN

# The analogue stick (ABS_X / ABS_Y, -127..127, flat 15) is deliberately NOT mapped.
# The conversion compares for EQUALITY with the declared min/max, so a direction would
# only register at exact full deflection and release at 126. Map it once that path
# takes a threshold.
